package Libraries.Language.Compile.Translate

use Libraries.Containers.Array
use Libraries.Containers.HashTable
use Libraries.Containers.Iterator
use Libraries.Language.Compile.Symbol.Class
use Libraries.Language.Compile.Symbol.Action
use Libraries.Language.Compile.Symbol.ActionCallResolution
use Libraries.Language.Compile.Symbol.SymbolTable
use Libraries.Language.Compile.CompilerError
use Libraries.Language.Compile.CompilerErrorType
use Libraries.Language.Compile.CompilerErrorCodes
use Libraries.Language.Compile.CompilerErrorManager
use Libraries.Language.Compile.Location

/*
    Works out which of a program's actions can wait (Action:CanWait), and
    reports the places that can't wait. Waiting comes from multitasking
    (Libraries.Multitasking): a task's actions and the lines that run them.

    An action that waits needs every caller to wait for it too, all the way
    up. How depends on the target: in JavaScript, and in Python mode, such
    actions are written async and every call to them is awaited; on Java
    the calling thread blocks, so nothing changes. The code writers read
    what it works out (Libraries.Language.Compile.Translate.ActionOpcode and
    Libraries.Language.Compile.Translate.ChainedActionCallOpcode read
    Action:CanWait).

    It works in three steps.

    1. It marks the multitasking library's actions (MarkLibraryActions):
       - The actions that wait: Libraries.Multitasking.Task's Wait and
         Pause; Libraries.Multitasking.Lines' Wait, WaitForAny and Pause;
         Libraries.Multitasking.Line's Wait; and Libraries.Multitasking.Key's
         ReturnAndWait. Wait, WaitForAny and ReturnAndWait come with and
         without a time limit; Pause always has one.
       - Libraries.Multitasking.Task's Run and Then. The multitasking library
         calls a task's Run, waits for it, then calls Then and waits for
         that, so a task's overrides of them may wait
         (Action:OverrideMayWait), and a call to either is awaited.
    2. It marks the program's actions that can wait: an action that calls one
       that can wait, and an action that a subclass overrides with one that
       can wait (a call through the parent's type may reach the override).
       This needs every action's calls, so it runs after the listener has
       gone through the whole program, and before any code is written. It
       walks outward from the actions that wait, so each action and each
       call is handled once.
    3. It reports the places that can't wait:
       - making an object: on create, and fields' starting values (a
         JavaScript constructor can't be async);
       - an override of a library action that the library calls without
         waiting (Action:OverrideMayWait is false), such as Compare.

    All of this is kept on the actions themselves, set in this one sweep
    before any code is written, so the writers only read it.
*/
class WaitAnalysis
    CompilerErrorCodes codes
    constant text TASK = "Libraries.Multitasking.Task"
    constant text LINES = "Libraries.Multitasking.Lines"
    constant text LINE = "Libraries.Multitasking.Line"
    constant text KEY = "Libraries.Multitasking.Key"

    /*
        This action marks which of a program's actions can wait, then
        reports the places that wait where they can't, in the three steps
        the class describes. It runs once per compile, after the listener
        has gone through every class and before any code is written.

        A program's flags are cleared first, because symbols can outlive a
        compile: Quorum Studio starts each build from the last one's symbol
        table, so an action that waited before an edit might not now.

        Attribute: Parameter classOpcodes The program's classes.
        Attribute: Parameter table The compile's symbol table, which also holds the standard library's classes.
        Attribute: Parameter errors Where errors are reported.
        Attribute: Returns false if it reported an error, so no code should be written, and true otherwise.
    */
    action Mark(Array<ClassOpcode> classOpcodes, SymbolTable table, CompilerErrorManager errors) returns boolean
        Array<Action> actions = GetActions(classOpcodes)

        integer i = 0
        repeat while i < actions:GetSize()
            Action act = actions:Get(i)
            act:SetCanWait(false)
            act:SetOverrideMayWait(false)
            i = i + 1
        end
        MarkLibraryActions(table)

        // Who calls each action, and the program's parent actions each
        // action overrides, found once.
        HashTable<text, Array<Action>> callers
        HashTable<text, Array<Action>> overridden
        Array<Action> work

        i = 0
        repeat while i < actions:GetSize()
            Action act = actions:Get(i)
            Iterator<ActionCallResolution> calls = act:GetActionCalls()
            repeat while calls:HasNext()
                ActionCallResolution call = calls:Next()
                Action called = call:resolvedAction
                if called not= undefined
                    AddTo(callers, GetStaticKey(called), act)
                    if called:CanWait() and not act:CanWait()
                        act:SetCanWait(true)
                        work:Add(act)
                    end
                end
            end

            Class owner = act:GetParentClass()
            Iterator<Class> parents = owner:GetParentClasses()
            repeat while parents:HasNext()
                Class parentClass = parents:Next()
                Action parentAction = OverriddenAction(parentClass, act)
                if parentAction not= undefined and not IsLibrary(parentClass)
                    AddTo(overridden, GetStaticKey(act), parentAction)
                end
            end
            i = i + 1
        end

        repeat while not work:IsEmpty()
            Action done = work:RemoveFromEnd()
            text key = GetStaticKey(done)
            MarkAll(callers, key, work)
            MarkAll(overridden, key, work)
        end

        boolean fine = true
        i = 0
        repeat while i < classOpcodes:GetSize()
            ClassOpcode opcode = classOpcodes:Get(i)
            Class clazz = opcode:GetClass()
            if not CheckMaking(clazz, errors)
                fine = false
            end
            i = i + 1
        end
        i = 0
        repeat while i < actions:GetSize()
            Action act = actions:Get(i)
            if act:CanWait() and not CheckLibraryOverrides(act, errors)
                fine = false
            end
            i = i + 1
        end
        return fine
    end

    /*
        This action marks the multitasking library's actions (step 1 in the
        class's description): the actions that wait get CanWait, and a
        task's Run and Then get both CanWait and OverrideMayWait. The
        library's actions that wait call only each other, never a program's
        actions, so none of this depends on the program. When multitasking
        is in the standard library, these flags are set on the library's
        own Action objects, which every compile shares; they stay set,
        which is right, since they never change.

        Attribute: Parameter table The compile's symbol table, where the multitasking classes are found.
    */
    private action MarkLibraryActions(SymbolTable table)
        MarkWaits(table, TASK, "Wait")
        MarkWaits(table, TASK, "Wait:number")
        MarkWaits(table, TASK, "Pause:number")
        MarkWaits(table, LINES, "Wait")
        MarkWaits(table, LINES, "Wait:number")
        MarkWaits(table, LINES, "WaitForAny")
        MarkWaits(table, LINES, "WaitForAny:number")
        MarkWaits(table, LINES, "Pause:number")
        MarkWaits(table, LINE, "Wait")
        MarkWaits(table, LINE, "Wait:number")
        MarkWaits(table, KEY, "ReturnAndWait")
        MarkWaits(table, KEY, "ReturnAndWait:number")
        MarkOverrideMayWait(table, TASK, "Run")
        MarkOverrideMayWait(table, TASK, "Then")
    end

    /*
        This action marks one library action as one that waits, so every
        call to it is awaited and every action that calls it can wait. If
        the program doesn't use the action's class, there is nothing to
        mark.

        Attribute: Parameter table The compile's symbol table.
        Attribute: Parameter classKey The static key of the action's class, such as Libraries.Multitasking.Task.
        Attribute: Parameter actionKey The action's static key: its name and its parameters' types, joined by colons, such as Wait:number.
    */
    private action MarkWaits(SymbolTable table, text classKey, text actionKey)
        Action act = Find(table, classKey, actionKey)
        if act not= undefined
            act:SetCanWait(true)
        end
    end

    /*
        This action marks one library action that the library calls and
        waits for, such as a task's Run. A program's override of it may wait
        (OverrideMayWait), and since a call to it may reach such an
        override, every call to it is awaited (CanWait).

        Attribute: Parameter table The compile's symbol table.
        Attribute: Parameter classKey The static key of the action's class.
        Attribute: Parameter actionKey The action's static key.
    */
    private action MarkOverrideMayWait(SymbolTable table, text classKey, text actionKey)
        Action act = Find(table, classKey, actionKey)
        if act not= undefined
            act:SetCanWait(true)
            act:SetOverrideMayWait(true)
        end
    end

    /*
        This action finds an action by its class's static key and its own,
        in the compile's symbol table.

        Attribute: Parameter table The compile's symbol table.
        Attribute: Parameter classKey The static key of the action's class.
        Attribute: Parameter actionKey The action's static key.
        Attribute: Returns The action, or undefined if the class isn't in the table or doesn't declare the action.
    */
    private action Find(SymbolTable table, text classKey, text actionKey) returns Action
        Class clazz = table:GetClass(classKey)
        if clazz = undefined or not clazz:HasAction(actionKey)
            return undefined
        end
        return clazz:GetAction(actionKey)
    end

    /*
        This action collects every action the program's classes declare,
        their constructors included, into one array, so Mark can go through
        them several times without walking the classes each time. The
        standard library's actions aren't included.

        Attribute: Parameter classOpcodes The program's classes.
        Attribute: Returns An array of the program's actions.
    */
    private action GetActions(Array<ClassOpcode> classOpcodes) returns Array<Action>
        Array<Action> actions
        integer i = 0
        repeat while i < classOpcodes:GetSize()
            ClassOpcode opcode = classOpcodes:Get(i)
            Class clazz = opcode:GetClass()
            Iterator<Action> owned = clazz:GetActions()
            repeat while owned:HasNext()
                actions:Add(owned:Next())
            end
            Action constructor = clazz:GetConstructor()
            if constructor not= undefined
                actions:Add(constructor)
            end
            i = i + 1
        end
        return actions
    end

    /*
        This action returns a static key that names an action across the
        whole program: its class's static key and its own, joined by a bar,
        such as Libraries.Multitasking.Task|Wait:number. An action's own
        static key is only unique within its class, so the class's is
        needed too. The tables in Mark are keyed by it.

        Attribute: Parameter act The action.
        Attribute: Returns The action's static key across the program.
    */
    private action GetStaticKey(Action act) returns text
        Class owner = act:GetParentClass()
        if owner = undefined
            return act:GetStaticKey()
        end
        return owner:GetStaticKey() + "|" + act:GetStaticKey()
    end

    /*
        This action adds an action to the array a table keeps under a key,
        making the array the first time the key is used. Mark's tables list,
        for each action, the actions that call it, or the program's parent
        actions it overrides.

        Attribute: Parameter table The table to add to.
        Attribute: Parameter key The key to add under (see GetStaticKey).
        Attribute: Parameter act The action to add.
    */
    private action AddTo(HashTable<text, Array<Action>> table, text key, Action act)
        Array<Action> list = undefined
        if table:HasKey(key)
            list = table:GetValue(key)
        else
            Array<Action> made
            list = made
            table:Add(key, list)
        end
        list:Add(act)
    end

    /*
        This action is one step of the walk outward from the actions that
        wait. It marks every action a table keeps under a key as one that can
        wait (for example, every action that calls the action just marked),
        and adds each one it newly marks to the work still to do, so its own
        callers are marked in turn. An action already marked is skipped, so
        each is handled once.

        Attribute: Parameter table The table to read (callers, or overridden actions).
        Attribute: Parameter key The static key of the action just marked (see GetStaticKey).
        Attribute: Parameter work The actions marked but not yet followed.
    */
    private action MarkAll(HashTable<text, Array<Action>> table, text key, Array<Action> work)
        if not table:HasKey(key)
            return now
        end
        Array<Action> list = table:GetValue(key)
        integer i = 0
        repeat while i < list:GetSize()
            Action act = list:Get(i)
            if not act:CanWait()
                act:SetCanWait(true)
                work:Add(act)
            end
            i = i + 1
        end
    end

    /*
        This action finds the action a parent class declares that the given
        action overrides: one with the same static key. A class can have
        several parents, and a parent's parents are its parents too
        (Class:GetParentClasses lists every one), so callers ask each in
        turn; more than one may declare the action, and each is found. A
        parent that only inherits the action doesn't count, since the parent
        that declares it is asked too.

        Attribute: Parameter parentClass One of the class's parents.
        Attribute: Parameter act The action that may override it.
        Attribute: Returns The parent's own action that act overrides, or undefined if the parent doesn't declare one.
    */
    private action OverriddenAction(Class parentClass, Action act) returns Action
        text key = act:GetStaticKey()
        if not parentClass:HasAction(key)
            return undefined
        end
        Action parentAction = parentClass:GetAction(key)
        Class declaredIn = parentAction:GetParentClass()
        if declaredIn = undefined or declaredIn:GetStaticKey() not= parentClass:GetStaticKey()
            return undefined
        end
        return parentAction
    end

    /*
        This action returns whether a class belongs to the standard library,
        which is compiled before any program and calls a program's overrides
        without waiting. That is a class compiled apart from the program, or
        one in the library's Libraries namespace, as multitasking is while
        it is compiled together with a program, before it joins the library.

        Attribute: Parameter clazz The class.
        Attribute: Returns true for a standard library class.
    */
    private action IsLibrary(Class clazz) returns boolean
        if not clazz:IsUserCode()
            return true
        end
        text key = clazz:GetStaticKey()
        return key:StartsWith("Libraries.")
    end

    /*
        This action finds the first call an action makes to an action that
        can wait, so an error can say why the action can wait ("it calls
        Wait, which can wait").

        Attribute: Parameter act The action.
        Attribute: Returns The first such call, or undefined if there is none.
    */
    private action FirstWaitingCall(Action act) returns ActionCallResolution
        Iterator<ActionCallResolution> calls = act:GetActionCalls()
        repeat while calls:HasNext()
            ActionCallResolution call = calls:Next()
            Action called = call:resolvedAction
            if called not= undefined and called:CanWait()
                return call
            end
        end
        return undefined
    end

    /*
        This action reports waiting while an object of a class is made,
        which can't wait: a JavaScript constructor can't be async. It checks
        the class's on create (its constructor), and the calls in its
        fields' starting values (Class:GetFieldActionCalls), which are set
        inside the constructor. Each call to an action that can wait is an
        error, reported where the call is.

        Attribute: Parameter clazz The class.
        Attribute: Parameter errors Where errors are reported.
        Attribute: Returns false if it reported an error, and true otherwise.
    */
    private action CheckMaking(Class clazz, CompilerErrorManager errors) returns boolean
        boolean fine = true
        Action constructor = clazz:GetConstructor()
        if constructor not= undefined and constructor:CanWait()
            ActionCallResolution call = FirstWaitingCall(constructor)
            Location where = constructor:GetHeaderLocation()
            text called = "an action that can wait"
            if call not= undefined
                where = call:location
                Action calledAction = call:resolvedAction
                called = calledAction:GetName() + ", which can wait"
            end
            Report(errors, where, "This calls " + called + ", but it runs while a "
                + clazz:GetName() + " is made, which can't wait. Call it from an action instead.")
            fine = false
        end
        Iterator<ActionCallResolution> calls = clazz:GetFieldActionCalls()
        repeat while calls:HasNext()
            ActionCallResolution call = calls:Next()
            Action calledAction = call:resolvedAction
            if calledAction not= undefined and calledAction:CanWait()
                Report(errors, call:location, "A field's starting value can't come from "
                    + calledAction:GetName() + ", which can wait: fields are set while a "
                    + clazz:GetName() + " is made, which can't wait. Set it in an action instead.")
                fine = false
            end
        end
        return fine
    end

    /*
        This action checks one of the program's actions that can wait, to
        see whether it overrides a library action that the library calls
        without waiting. If it does, that is an error.

        Why: the standard library is compiled before any program, so its
        code calls a program's overrides as ordinary actions and uses what
        they return right away. It can't wait for an override that waits: in
        JavaScript, it would get an unfinished promise instead of the
        result. Only the library actions the library is built to wait for,
        a task's Run and Then (Action:OverrideMayWait), may be overridden by
        actions that wait.

        An example. Here Ranked's Compare can wait, because it calls Wait:

            class Ranked
                Task check
                action Compare(Object object) returns integer
                    check:Wait()
                    return 0
                end
            end

        Ranked's parents include Libraries.Language.Object, a library class
        that declares the Compare that Ranked's Compare overrides. That
        Compare doesn't allow waiting, because Sort calls it in the middle of
        sorting and needs the answer at once. So this reports an error at
        Ranked's Compare. By contrast, if Ranked were a task (Ranked is
        Task) and the action that waits were its Run, the Run it overrides
        is Libraries.Multitasking.Task's, which allows waiting, so nothing
        would be reported.

        How: it goes through every parent of the action's class. For each
        library parent that declares the action this one overrides
        (OverriddenAction), it checks whether that action allows waiting,
        and reports the first that doesn't, once, at the action's header.
        Library classes' own actions aren't checked: the library's code is
        written to wait where it needs to.

        Attribute: Parameter act One of the program's actions that can wait.
        Attribute: Parameter errors Where errors are reported.
        Attribute: Returns false if it reported an error, and true otherwise.
    */
    private action CheckLibraryOverrides(Action act, CompilerErrorManager errors) returns boolean
        Class owner = act:GetParentClass()
        if IsLibrary(owner)
            return true
        end
        Iterator<Class> parents = owner:GetParentClasses()
        repeat while parents:HasNext()
            Class parentClass = parents:Next()
            Action parentAction = OverriddenAction(parentClass, act)
            if parentAction not= undefined and IsLibrary(parentClass)
                and not parentAction:OverrideMayWait()
                text why = "it waits"
                ActionCallResolution call = FirstWaitingCall(act)
                if call not= undefined
                    Action calledAction = call:resolvedAction
                    why = "it calls " + calledAction:GetName() + ", which can wait"
                end
                Report(errors, act:GetHeaderLocation(), act:GetName() + " can wait, because " + why
                    + ". It overrides " + parentClass:GetStaticKey() + "'s " + act:GetName()
                    + ", which the library calls without waiting, so it may not wait. Start the work"
                    + " with a Lines object's LineUp, and collect the result in a task's Then or by"
                    + " checking IsFinished.")
                return false
            end
        end
        return true
    end

    /*
        This action adds an error for waiting where it can't, with this
        class's error code (CompilerErrorCodes:WAIT_WHERE_IT_CANNOT_WAIT).

        Attribute: Parameter errors Where the error is reported.
        Attribute: Parameter location Where in the program the problem is.
        Attribute: Parameter message What is wrong, and what to do instead.
    */
    private action Report(CompilerErrorManager errors, Location location, text message)
        CompilerError error
        error:SetCode(codes:WAIT_WHERE_IT_CANNOT_WAIT)
        error:SetLocation(location)
        error:SetErrorMessage(message)
        CompilerErrorType errorType
        errorType:SetCurrentType(errorType:OTHER)
        error:SetCompilerErrorType(errorType)
        errors:Add(error)
    end
end
